    {
      "id": "7cjyrs5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Article 12–13: Definition and Protection"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s2uillc",
      "content": "• Article 12 defines the term 'State'. It includes Government, Parliament, State Legislatures, local authorities and other authorities."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w6aw7v0",
      "content": "• Article 13 declares that laws inconsistent with Fundamental Rights are void."
    },
    {
      "id": "wne5nx8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Right to Equality (Articles 14–18)"
    },
    {
      "id": "v63q69m",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Article</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Provision</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 14</p>",
            "<p>Equality before law and equal protection of laws</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 15</p>",
            "<p>Prohibition of discrimination on grounds of religion, race, caste, sex or place of birth</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 16</p>",
            "<p>Equality of opportunity in public employment</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 17</p>",
            "<p>Abolition of untouchability</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Article 18</p>",
            "<p>Abolition of titles</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2yw09np",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Exceptions to Right to Equality"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zdg7ofe",
      "content": "• President and Governors enjoy immunity from court proceedings during their tenure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ubg91sy",
      "content": "• Parliament can make special provisions for women and children."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sziq4b7",
      "content": "• State can provide reservations for SC, ST and OBC."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4arq8k0",
      "content": "• Diplomatic officials enjoy immunity."
    },
    {
      "id": "d1kpwgi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Right to Freedom (Articles 19–22)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jdsvctb",
      "content": "Article 19 provides six freedoms to citizens:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ickt1xt",
      "content": "• Freedom of speech and expression"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "tjaitbo",
      "content": "• Freedom to assemble peacefully"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "49jmi30",
      "content": "• Freedom to form associations or unions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "o04qem3",
      "content": "• Freedom to move freely throughout India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oq3m3tq",
      "content": "• Freedom to reside and settle in any part of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "umbqvgy",
      "content": "• Freedom to practice any profession or occupation"
    },
    {
      "id": "00xzh04",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Reasonable Restrictions"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qancf55",
      "content": "• Security of the state"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hqx6omg",
      "content": "• Public order"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "rcf55si",
      "content": "• Morality"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gr8n4r5",
      "content": "• Friendly relations with foreign states"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "w3s4i23",
      "content": "• Contempt of court"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0szzph4",
      "content": "• Defamation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ocgeste",
      "content": "Article 20 protects against arbitrary punishment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pok8a5k",
      "content": "Article 21 guarantees protection of life and personal liberty."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5uli9ww",
      "content": "Article 21A provides the Right to Education (added by 86th Amendment)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "csjh51w",
      "content": "Article 22 protects against arbitrary arrest and detention."
    },
    {
      "id": "nhg4zc9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Right against Exploitation (Articles 23–24)"
    },
